# Image resolver provider keys.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values you want enabled.
# All providers gracefully no-op when their key is missing — the resolver
# falls through to the next source (Wikipedia → curated fallback).

# Unsplash (browser-friendly, search-by-text).
# Get a key: https://unsplash.com/developers
# VITE_UNSPLASH_KEY=

# Google Places (production needs a small server proxy because direct
# browser calls are blocked by CORS). Set the proxy base URL below;
# the proxy is expected to expose `GET /photo?query=...` returning
# `{ image_url: "..." }`.
# VITE_PLACES_PROXY_URL=
# VITE_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=

# Anthropic key — when wiring Claude into lib/ai/generateTrip.js.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Base URL for the auth/API server (server/).
#
# Local dev: defaults to http://localhost:4000/api when unset. You only need
# to set this if you proxy through a different host.
#
# Production hosts: REQUIRED. Set this to the public URL of your deployed
# Express backend, e.g. https://api.your-domain.com/api. If you forget, the
# deployed frontend will try to hit localhost from the visitor's browser and
# every request will fail with "Failed to fetch". Configure this in your
# host's environment-variable UI for production / preview environments and
# redeploy.
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api
